The bug was in `advanceTurn` in `src/sim.ts`. The population-growth condition was `foodSurplus >= 0`, which incremented population even when production exactly equaled consumption (surplus = 0). Per the spec, population should only grow on an actual surplus.

Fixed by changing the condition to `foodSurplus > 0` (strict surplus). Verified in the file: the conditional on line 43 now reads `if (foodSurplus > 0) { population += 1; }`, and the rest of the function is unchanged. No source files were modified beyond this single line; no fixture or benchmark artifacts were touched.


